What About Different Objects With the Same Hash?

Same hash
      ≠
Same object
      ≠
Equal object

===========================
A Python set is implemented using a hash-table-based data structure and maintains
a uniqueness invariant. When an element is inserted, Python uses its hash to
locate the relevant table position and then uses equality comparison to determine
whether an equivalent element already exists. If an equal, hash-compatible element
is already present, the insertion doesn't create another entry. This gives sets
average O(1) membership and insertion while guaranteeing uniqueness according to
the object's equality/hash semantics.
